{
  "model": "models/SettingsComposition.tla",
  "scope": "finite protocol model: 2 target/authority changes plus 1 assignment change, 2 readers, 1 write; no implementation, liveness, isolation, catalog paging or physical durability proof; StandingCommit: two operations, one membership and one invalidation; abstract atomic stores; safety only, no remote authentication or physical durability proof; SettingsSourceRetention: two destinations, two source updates, one crash; safety and conditional progress under eventual storage availability and weakly fair recovery; fixed identity bindings, abstract atomic source transactions, no production refinement proof; source write conditions abstract confirmed final business validity as a monotone boolean, not a schema or original binding proof; SettingsSourceIdentity: two ordered sources, four identity/layout replacements, one authority refresh, one prepare/write/rebase; finite safety only, authenticated ownership and SQL isolation are assumptions SettingsIntentAttempts checks finite root/attempt safety with two allowed attempts, immutable commands, exact current attempt, read-only queries and distinct ordinary/source sealing. No liveness or real provider guarantee. SettingsPreparationBootstrap models one durable attempt, two external reservations and one restart; safety only. External owners serialize reserve/settle and validate exact reservation bindings; SQL transactions and authentic providers are assumptions, not proved implementations. SettingsReservationCustody models one destination and two candidate request identities with lost/delayed replies; finite safety only. Authentic external replies, external idempotent reserve, and atomic journal writes are assumptions. StandingRequestSettlement: one original request, two candidate bindings, one delayed reserve and one restart; safety and conditional progress under weakly fair trusted settlement; source/destination atomic transactions and immutable SQL envelopes are assumptions, not implementation proofs.",
